WEBVTT

NOTE The video has no audio. These cues repeat the on-screen text. Generated from src/scenes.js.

1
00:00:00.400 --> 00:00:03.700
AI was supposed to save us time.

2
00:00:03.700 --> 00:00:07.900
So why can coding with it still feel so tiring?

3
00:00:08.000 --> 00:00:11.300
An agent can write code in minutes.

4
00:00:11.300 --> 00:00:14.700
It can run many tasks at once.

5
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.300
Each result still asks something of a person.

6
00:00:19.300 --> 00:00:23.500
More output does not give us more attention.

7
00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.500
What can we hand off? What must stay ours?

8
00:00:27.500 --> 00:00:31.200
Let AI help with drafts, tests, and ideas.

9
00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:36.400
Keep the judgment: what matters, what is good enough, and who owns it.

10
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:41.000
When there is always more, it is easy to push harder.

11
00:00:41.000 --> 00:00:45.600
Notice it: “I am tired, and there is a lot to review.”

12
00:00:45.600 --> 00:00:50.200
Remember: struggling is not a private failure. Many people feel this.

13
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:54.600
Be kind: choose a limit, as you would for a friend.

14
00:00:56.100 --> 00:01:01.300
Tools that help us do more need a partner that helps us pause.

15
00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:06.400
Cukup counts each Amp turn, plus 15 minutes after it.

16
00:01:06.400 --> 00:01:11.400
Across this synthetic day, that gives 8h 7m. The target is 8h 0m.

17
00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:14.800
It is an estimate, not measured attention.

18
00:01:14.800 --> 00:01:19.200
It is one prompt to ask: is this enough for today?

19
00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:22.600
Cukup does not decide. You do.

20
00:01:23.200 --> 00:01:26.300
Let AI help you do the work.

21
00:01:26.300 --> 00:01:29.700
Keep the decision to say: cukup.

22
00:01:29.700 --> 00:01:33.900
cukup.dev
A personal dashboard · Amp only · Open-source release in preparation
